  "text_to_speech": "okay so this video shows how to connect Android phone to Smart TV then share phone screen with Smart TV so we can play games and videos so we can play in full screen so I will show you how we can configure this first we need to connect our mobile phone and Smart TV to save Wi-Fi network so in your smart TV just go to the network then select Wi-Fi wireless connection then select the Wi-Fi network which you want to connect in my case it is my Wi-Fi then enter the password then save it we can see it's connecting okay connected done in your mobile phone go to settings tap on settings then tap on Wi-Fi then from available networks you have to select the Wi-Fi network so just select the same Wi-Fi network which you connected to your smart TV so in my case this is my Wi-Fi tap on that and enter the password tap on connect okay it's connected if you can see Wi-Fi as connected to my Wi-Fi Network then again go to settings then tap on more tap on wireless display then turn on wireless display tap on a wireless display so we can turn it on so now we turned on wireless display then in your smart TV open Miracast app so you can see Miracast app here open this Miracast app okay you can see it's waiting for the user to connect launch wireless display on your device now in your mobile phone we would be able to see the name of your smart TV can see Smart TV tap on that you can see it's connecting okay connected so this way we can share your Mobile screen with your smart TV and you can play games and videos I hope you enjoyed this video please subscribe my Channel please like and share the video so if you have any doubt please comment",
